            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0284" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg188"/>

                <head>No. 137.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bancroft to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-04-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 9, 1872</date>. (Received April
                        25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 351.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Germana Parliament was opened yesterday
                    by Prince Bismarck. <pb facs="0285" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/> Notice was made in
                    the Emperor’s speech of the consular treaty with the United States, which will
                    be at once laid before Parliament, and undoubtedly receive its approbation.
                    Nothing else in the speech deserves your particular attention, except the
                    reiterated assertion that the unity of Germany is a guarantee of the peace of
                    Europe.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
